.TH CSTRING_GET_MPROCS 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Functions"
.SH NAME
cstring_get_mprocs \- get the memory management procedures for a string
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cstring.h>

ccol_memmgmt_procs_t *cstring_get_mprocs(cstr s);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
This function returns the custom memory management procedures that the
string was created with, or NULL when the string uses the default
malloc/free allocators.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
s   String to query
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
A pointer to the memory management procedures, or NULL for the defaults
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
The structure belongs to the library and stays valid until the string is
destroyed. Do not free it yourself, and do not use it after the destroy
Asserts if s is NULL
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cstring_create_full (3)
